 "user": {"id": 13656, "username": "blindrepublic", "name": "b r", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/b/db3279/{size}.png", "trust_level": 1}}, {"extras": "latest", "description": "Most Recent Poster", "user": {"id": 16855, "username": "chrisawi", "name": "Chris Williams", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/eb7434/{size}.png", "trust_level": 2}}]}], "summarizable": false, "has_cached_summary": false, "has_livestream": null, "valid_reactions": ["heart", "classic_smiley", "bluethumb", "party", "eureka", "totally", "fedora", "eyes"], "accepted_answers": [{"id": 157267, "name": "lordpipe", "username": "lordpipe", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/lordpipe/{size}/10071_2.png", "created_at": "2022-10-07T19:31:24.757Z", "cooked": "<p>Oh, it was! Not sure how I missed that.</p>\n<p>So the solution was</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-bash\">dnf remove xdg-desktop-portal-gnome\n</code></pre>\n<p>Note to anyone trying to remove <code>xdg-desktop-portal-gnome</code> — I had to relog after doing it. It will be broken until you log back into your session.</p>\n<p>This fixed the file picker, but for some reason the KDE Qt theme is still not applying for some flatpaks, such as Calibre.</p>", "post_number": 5, "topic_id": 70249, "url": "/t/flatpak-applications-are-suddenly-using-the-gtk-file-picker-instead-of-qt-how-do-i-change-it-back/70249/5"}], "has_accepted_answer": true, "shared_issue_count": 0, "can_create_shared_issue": false, "shared_issue_visible": true, "discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_id": null, "discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_url": "https://your-url.zendesk.com/agent/tickets/", "details": {"can_edit": false, "notification_level": 1, "participants": [{"id": 12298, "username": "lordpipe", "name": "lordpipe", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/lordpipe/{size}/10071_2.png", "post_count": 6, "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flai